WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.220
We have to talk about the so-called Muslim
ban today.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:17.270
Before I say anything else I want to be crystal
clear on one fact: I am absolutely against

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:23.350
any ban on immigrants based solely on their
religion, whatever religion that may be.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:28.160
I will always judge people as individuals,
not as a collective, and I certainly don't

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.730
plan on stopping now as this fight over refugees
and immigration is just heating up.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:40.719
Within any group there are sub groups of people,
and often these sub groups contain the most

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:45.569
vulnerable populations such as free thinkers,
gays, and atheists.

00:00:45.569 --> 00:00:54.249
Just so the trolls get it right: I, Dave Rubin,
am 100% against any blanket ban which targets

00:00:54.249 --> 00:01:01.359
all Muslim people, and I would feel exactly
the same way if it was targeting other religion.

00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:09.580
Now, this refugee issue is one of those topics
where, no matter what I say, I will get hate

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.250
from both the extreme left and the extreme
right.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:17.520
Actually, the more I get hate from both sides
the more I realize I'm doing the right thing

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:24.190
because nuance, honesty and logic are lost
on those who stay on the dogmatic fringes.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:31.630
So, before I share my thoughts, I think it's
important we separate some fact from fiction

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:35.930
and discuss what's actually in Trump's executive
order.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:40.790
I've got the whole text of the order right
here and yes, I read the whole order, unlike

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:44.760
most of the people screaming about it online.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:50.870
Despite what the hashtag on Twitter might
tell you, this is not a Muslim Ban.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:55.480
First off, The word Muslim isn't in the text
of the order, not even once -- you'd think

00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:00.450
if you were exclusively trying to ban people
of one religion from entering the country,

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.200
you'd have to cite which religion you're talking
about.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:09.700
Secondly, and perhaps more importantly, the
ban doesn't include any of the five most populous

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:14.490
Muslim countries: Indonesia, India, Pakistan,
Bangladesh and and Nigeria.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:19.930
So, if this was exclusively a Muslim ban,
it does stand to reason it would include these

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:25.720
countries, which adds up to roughly 750 million
people.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:30.700
So if it is a Muslim ban, it's excluding more
than half of the Muslims in the world.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:35.120
This doesn't mean there aren't some valid
questions about the list of which countries

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.290
are banned, as well as some glaring omissions
of this executive order.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:46.900
The 7 countries listed are: Syria, Libya,
Sudan, Iran, Yemen, Somalia and Iraq.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:50.980
All of these countries are involved in heavy
sectarian violence, some of which is a direct

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:54.820
result of American intervention, without question.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:03:00.520
To be clear though, no major terrorist attack
has happened on American soil from anyone

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:03.920
from the 7 countries currently on the banned
list.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:09.740
At the same time there are omissions on the
list, most notably Saudi Arabia, which 19

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:13.000
of the 21 9/11 hijackers were from.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.170
The argument I've heard on this is that the
ban applies to current conflict zones, and

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:21.850
as odious as the Saudi government may be,
the country isn't a war zone.

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:26.760
I don't see how this is related to whether
extremists are coming out of the country,

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.910
actually we know they have in the past and
continue to do so, but that seems to be the

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.750
argument being made.

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:37.010
There are also many questions as to whether
Trump's business ties in countries like Turkey

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:41.890
and Saudi Arabia were at least part of the
reason that they were left off the list.

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:46.700
We know for a fact that Turkey is letting
ISIS fighters into Europe through it's border

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:53.080
and Saudi Arabia is the home to the worlds
most fervent stand of Sunni Wahhabism.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:58.160
So quick recap so far, we have a ban on nationals
from countries which are currently hot beds

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:04.170
for terrorism, though the list is incomplete
at best and arbitrary or ill conceived at

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:05.510
worst.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:08.900
Next is whether this is an actual ban or not.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:15.290
From reading the document itself as well as
analysis from other sources I generally trust,

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:23.030
there is in no way this order, at the moment,
is some kind of permanent ban on the people

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:24.280
from the countries listed.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:31.720
It's a 90 day ban on people from those 7 countries
and a total temporary stop of our refugee

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:38.630
admission system for 120 days so the vetting
system and other processes can be reviewed.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:45.190
The one exception to this temporary stop is
for Syrian refugees, who are banned indefinitely.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:49.040
Perhaps this will lead to Trump trying to
actually ban all foreign nationals from these

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:55.210
countries or even expanding it to other countries,
but at the moment, it is a temporary ban while

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.870
we figure out what's going on at our borders.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:02.940
Simply put, whether you like it or not, this
is one of the promises Trump made.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:08.860
If at the end of the 120 days we have a stronger
vetting process not based on blanket bigotry

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:14.360
but rather on informed decisions about each
person individually, then we can start to

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:19.370
have an honest discussion about how many refugees
we can or should let in.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:24.190
On the extremes we now have people calling
for totally open borders which is national

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:29.470
suicide, and we have other people calling
for zero immigration which is the antithesis

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:31.870
of what America stands for.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:36.740
Another important piece of the order is the
deference is being given to religious minorities

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:38.120
who are under persecution.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:41.270
I find the anger against this quite confusing.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:46.400
The left is supposed to be for minorities,
but in this case, giving priority to Yazidi,

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:51.240
Kurds, Christians and others who are being
wiped out as we speak, is somehow being turned

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:54.510
flipped as if this is supposedly anti Muslim.

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:59.130
The truth is these religious minorities are
the most vulnerable communities.

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:03.960
It doesn't matter if you're a believer or
a non believer to understand that protecting

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.510
the most at risk is the right thing to do.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:12.680
An interesting point to add here is the Obama
administration let in 12,000 Muslims from

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:16.830
Syria in 2016, but only 100 Christian refugees.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:21.150
I don't know the reasoning behind his policy,
but where was the outrage when Obama left

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:27.199
Christians behind, if this current outrage
truly is about protecting minorities who are

00:06:27.199 --> 00:06:28.940
in harms way?

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:34.890
The order also limits the amount of refugees
to 50,000 per year which is basically in line

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:38.470
with where we've been over the past 15 years
or so.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:45.230
For example in 2003, 2006 and 2007, we admitted
less than 50,00 refugees per year under George

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:46.460
W. Bush.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:52.620
Obama bumped up admitted refugees to 70,000
people in the last two years of his administration,

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:58.350
but in the previous three years before that
he was right around 50,00 as well.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:03.199
Without getting too lose in the numbers here,
the point is, Trump's proposal isn't far off

00:07:03.199 --> 00:07:08.890
previous administrations, especially if you
remove the bump in the last two years under

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:09.890
Obama.

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:14.470
Of course you could argue American action
or inaction in Syria has led to many of these

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:16.310
refugees in the first place.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:20.890
So again, where was the outrage when we were
dropping bombs, not just temporarily limiting

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:23.020
refugees.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:28.100
Of course the last few years also coincide
with a jump in world wide jihad especially

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.639
in countries which have taken in many refugees.

00:07:30.639 --> 00:07:35.610
I think if you could ask the people of Germany,
France, and Belgium if they might rethink

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:40.840
some of their immigration policies over the
past few years there would be a resounding

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:41.840
yes.

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:47.270
These countries now have to deal with homegrown
terror as well as the influx of refugees which

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:51.760
has created a new set of problems both economically
and culturally.

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:58.190
None of this is a reason not to let sensible
amounts of properly vetted refugees in, but

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:04.550
it does lend credence to a temporary pause
while we figure out if our vetting is effective

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.460
seems fairly sensible.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:12.020
The rollout of the order was no doubt absolutely
chaotic and confusing but I'm not sure if

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:16.819
any real change to our system could be done
without a certain amount of chaos and confusion,

00:08:16.819 --> 00:08:21.220
especially because of a media that thrives
on emotion over fact.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:25.120
Finally, there also seems to be some confusion
as to whether people who currently reside

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:28.520
in the United States with green cards from
these 7 countries mentioned in the order would

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:31.759
be able to leave the country and come back.

00:08:31.759 --> 00:08:36.430
At first it sounded like they couldn't get
back in, then it sounded like yes, now it

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:39.479
sounds like a case by case basis.

00:08:39.479 --> 00:08:44.740
For example, my friend and former guest Faisal
al Mutar, who is a refugee from Iraq who now

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:51.300
lives in America and has devoted his lives
to fighting Islamist and for secularism, could

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.940
possibly be locked out of the country if he
was to go do a speaking gig in Canada with

00:08:55.940 --> 00:09:00.209
my friend and former guest Ali Rizvi, a Muslim
reformer.

00:09:00.209 --> 00:09:04.260
This portion of the order still seems to be
in flux, which is evidence of a unprepared

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:05.740
roll out.

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:11.750
Of course this is 2017 and facts seems to
take a back seat to fiction and hysteria at

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:12.750
every turn.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:16.950
So some protesters are protesting without
really knowing what's happening.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:22.140
New York Senator Chuck Schumer is crying and
talking about a Muslim ban when he knows full

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:24.890
well that isn't what this is.

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:29.440
People are now drinking more Starbucks or
boycotting Starbucks because Starbucks CEO

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:32.410
Howard Shultz said he would hire 10,000 refugees.

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:37.970
Elon Musk, who publicly offered on Twitter
to take people's concerns directly to Trump

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:41.779
is being attacked by people as if he's enabling
a Nazi.

00:09:41.779 --> 00:09:46.900
As I predicted a few weeks ago, misguided
outrage is taking the place of real discussion.

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:51.470
So when politicians scream about a Muslim
ban, which this is not, it feeds the fire

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:56.520
to Trump to do whatever he wants, because
no matter what he does he knows they are going

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:57.940
to be outraged.

00:09:57.940 --> 00:10:01.830
This is why the regressive left and the Trumpian
right are the match made in hell for each

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:02.830
other.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:07.920
We have one side which refuses to debate Islamism
and immigration honestly and another side

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:13.010
that will be all to happy to use circumvent
our intended legislative process with the

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:14.530
stroke of a pen.

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:19.870
If you value liberty over authoritarianism,
then neither of these positions are tenable.

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:23.320
In an effort to make sense of some of the
madness surrounding the executive order, I

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:26.980
have a few interesting conversations planned
for this week, and I also want to share two

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:32.170
articles by people I truly respect, thought
they are often at opposite ends of the political

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:33.170
spectrum.

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:37.500
Below you can find links to an article Ben
Shapiro wrote about the order, as well as

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:39.820
a blog post by Sam Harris.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:44.140
In addition to those sources, in case you
missed it, I did a live stream with Faisal,

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:49.060
who is directly affected by this order, and
you can find a link to that below as well.

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:54.700
And finally, my guest this week is no stranger
to controversy and also someone who often

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:59.230
finds himself in the crosshairs of people
on both extremes.

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:03.670
Glenn Beck will be joining me in studio today
to discuss refugees, Trumpism, the modern

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:06.170
conservative movement, online media and more.

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:10.899
I agree with Glenn on some issue and disagree
with him on other but generally find him to

00:11:10.899 --> 00:11:14.550
be willing to have the hard conversations,
which right now we need more than ever.

